Module 3.2: Data Version Control (DVC)
Theory: Git doesn't handle large datasets. DVC versions data files using Git for metadata + remote storage (S3, GCS, Azure) for actual files.

Practice + Code:

```bash
# Initialize DVC
dvc init
git commit -m "Initialize DVC"

# Track a dataset
dvc add data/processed/train.csv
git add data/processed/train.csv.dvc .gitignore
git commit -m "Add training data v1.0"

# Simulate data update
# (modify train.csv)
